(408608, 35354, 656, '<td valign="top">the grey and gold work well together.  The shifting light through the water also works.  The couple of highlights and bubbles spoil it a bit for me in bringing it back to more concrete reality than the rest of the abstract showed.  I like it, but seem dissatisfied for some reason I can''t quite articulate.</td>', 'the grey and gold work well together.  The shifting light through the water also works.  The couple of highlights and bubbles spoil it a bit for me in bringing it back to more concrete reality than the rest of the abstract showed.  I like it, but seem dissatisfied for some reason I can''t quite articulate.', '2003-09-03 15:47:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(408624, 35761, 656, '<td valign="top">good colour choices, working well together.  I''m really pleased that there isn''t anytihng breaking up the pattern at the edges, but I can''t help feeling that a red piece in say the upper left blue row would make it more dramatic</td>', 'good colour choices, working well together.  I''m really pleased that there isn''t anytihng breaking up the pattern at the edges, but I can''t help feeling that a red piece in say the upper left blue row would make it more dramatic', '2003-09-03 15:51:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(408761, 35863, 10883, '<td valign="top">Great picture! - 8</td>', 'Great picture! - 8', '2003-09-03 17:15:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(408779, 35354, 7969, '<td valign="top">The light dances through the water creating a ballet of image for the eyes. The golden color weaving thru the blue the tones forming a tension of  balance and contrast simultaneously.  The light in the bubble and the downward line coming from it strikes me in as the ''star'' of this ballet. The movement here is elegant and graceful yet dynamic and powerful.  Excellent job, a  feast for the eyes!</td>', 'The light dances through the water creating a ballet of image for the eyes. The golden color weaving thru the blue the tones forming a tension of  balance and contrast simultaneously.  The light in the bubble and the downward line coming from it strikes me in as the ''star'' of this ballet. The movement here is elegant and graceful yet dynamic and powerful.  Excellent job, a  feast for the eyes!', '2003-09-03 17:26:37.000000', NULL, 1),
