(413097, 35507, 2000, '<td valign="top">**Critique Club**<br/>First Impression: Very dark, and that made it take a few seconds to see the hay bales, which I''m assuming is your repetition factor here.<br/> <br/>Composition/Technical: Again, it''s dark.  I agree with the comment already provided about cropping this slightly higher on the bottom, although I think a greater effect would be to crop some of the top away.  Given that you provide no explanation of this photograph, it''s difficult to discern what you were really going for here.<br/> <br/>Overall: If it is the hay you were shooting, it captures the essence of the challenge.  However, as it''s difficult to see, judging the quality of the repetition portion of the photograph is tough.  Good effort.<br/> <br/>Thanks for sharing, and good luck in future challenges. -Steve</td>', '**Critique Club**First Impression: Very dark, and that made it take a few seconds to see the hay bales, which I''m assuming is your repetition factor here. Composition/Technical: Again, it''s dark.  I agree with the comment already provided about cropping this slightly higher on the bottom, although I think a greater effect would be to crop some of the top away.  Given that you provide no explanation of this photograph, it''s difficult to discern what you were really going for here. Overall: If it is the hay you were shooting, it captures the essence of the challenge.  However, as it''s difficult to see, judging the quality of the repetition portion of the photograph is tough.  Good effort. Thanks for sharing, and good luck in future challenges. -Steve', '2003-09-08 22:57:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(413115, 35857, 7350, '<td valign="top">I scored this a 9.  I thought it was fantastic, and should have placed higher.  The lighting is perfect, the repetition makes the shot great instead of just being repetition for the challenge''s sake.  The cherry on top is the physical position of the woman as she takes a tired step down the long hallway.  Congratulations on a fantastic shot.</td>', 'I scored this a 9.  I thought it was fantastic, and should have placed higher.  The lighting is perfect, the repetition makes the shot great instead of just being repetition for the challenge''s sake.  The cherry on top is the physical position of the woman as she takes a tired step down the long hallway.  Congratulations on a fantastic shot.', '2003-09-08 23:58:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(413116, 35763, 656, '<td valign="top">My fav in this challenge</td>', 'My fav in this challenge', '2003-09-08 23:58:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(413156, 35857, 11184, '<td valign="top">Like many of the submissions, although there were lots of repetative objects in the shot they seemed more incidental and didn''t really seem to be the true subject of the shot nor really genuinely capture the theme.  You probably wouldn''t look at this photo and immediately say "repetition!"  If anything the stronger repetition theme for me might come in thinking about the repetition of the woman and her day  somehow.  <br/>However, this is SUCH a wonderful photo it probably would do extrememely well in lots of submission themes.  Would make a beautiful print.  Another fantastic shot for your terrific portfolio.</td>', 'Like many of the submissions, although there were lots of repetative objects in the shot they seemed more incidental and didn''t really seem to be the true subject of the shot nor really genuinely capture the theme.  You probably wouldn''t look at this photo and immediately say "repetition!"  If anything the stronger repetition theme for me might come in thinking about the repetition of the woman and her day  somehow.  However, this is SUCH a wonderful photo it probably would do extrememely well in lots of submission themes.  Would make a beautiful print.  Another fantastic shot for your terrific portfolio.', '2003-09-09 01:14:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(413163, 35911, 11184, '<td valign="top">I dunno, I kinda find that big white scrape in the foreground a bit too dominant and distracting...maybe try cropping in a row?  Absolutely brilliant shot though.  I want to be there...atleast the way you captured it.  One of those wonderful photos that you can almost feel and hear.</td>', 'I dunno, I kinda find that big white scrape in the foreground a bit too dominant and distracting...maybe try cropping in a row?  Absolutely brilliant shot though.  I want to be there...atleast the way you captured it.  One of those wonderful photos that you can almost feel and hear.', '2003-09-09 01:25:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(413240, 35943, 9073, '<td valign="top">I liked this shot, but didn''t have time to vote last week. You deserved a high score just for the title alone. On top of that, your kid is so cute, and her expression really pushes your point home. Maybe a little dark, though. <br/> <br/>Now, I''ll have that whining "are we there yet?" in my ears all day.  :(<br/> <br/> <br/>:)</td>', 'I liked this shot, but didn''t have time to vote last week. You deserved a high score just for the title alone. On top of that, your kid is so cute, and her expression really pushes your point home. Maybe a little dark, though.  Now, I''ll have that whining "are we there yet?" in my ears all day.  :(  :)', '2003-09-09 03:55:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(413352, 35784, 8643, '<td valign="top">Thank you commentators - you make the effort worthwhile.  There were some really good photos this challenge which did well and a few that weren''t so good that did well too, as usual.  It is all in the eye of the beholder.<br/>I shall keep trying and as long as I please myself and a few of you (and learn a bit too), all is well.<br/>Thank you!</td>', 'Thank you commentators - you make the effort worthwhile.  There were some really good photos this challenge which did well and a few that weren''t so good that did well too, as usual.  It is all in the eye of the beholder.I shall keep trying and as long as I please myself and a few of you (and learn a bit too), all is well.Thank you!', '2003-09-09 10:58:18.000000', NULL, 0),
