(414977, 35418, 9576, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ivar:</b></div><hr/><i>Sorry but I don´t get the repetition here...</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Just one of many morning papers you know 1.2.3...<br/>and this number 221 91th year. Er það ekki:-)</td>', 'Originally posted by Ivar:Sorry but I don´t get the repetition here... Just one of many morning papers you know 1.2.3...and this number 221 91th year. Er það ekki:-)', '2003-09-10 17:35:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(414981, 35418, 9576, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by FranziskaLang:</b></div><hr/><i>Another icelandic contribution I think :)  Without the challenge topic, repetition wouldn''t have been the first thing to come to mind, although I can see with the title and everything what you mean.  The pic is a little smaller than I''d like to see but the focus and use of DOF is fantastic,  I also like the border :)  Maybe use a plainer background in the bottom left corner (or just go with b&amp;w to deemphasize it) and I think you''ve done a bit too much contrast adjustment, the corners at the top are blown out.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Just one of many morning papers you know 1.2.3...<br/>and this number 221 91th year.<br/>Sorry that it is not bigger. I have it bigger but made some mistage when I send it <i>text</i></td>', 'Originally posted by FranziskaLang:Another icelandic contribution I think :)  Without the challenge topic, repetition wouldn''t have been the first thing to come to mind, although I can see with the title and everything what you mean.  The pic is a little smaller than I''d like to see but the focus and use of DOF is fantastic,  I also like the border :)  Maybe use a plainer background in the bottom left corner (or just go with b&w to deemphasize it) and I think you''ve done a bit too much contrast adjustment, the corners at the top are blown out. Just one of many morning papers you know 1.2.3...and this number 221 91th year.Sorry that it is not bigger. I have it bigger but made some mistage when I send it text', '2003-09-10 17:38:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(415625, 35911, 12088, '<td valign="top">good picture<br/>I like it</td>', 'good pictureI like it', '2003-09-11 06:08:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(415964, 35354, 7778, '<td valign="top">For those, who wanted to know what it was: a branch of an old ebony tree carefully painted with leaf-gold placed on a slab of BC jade submerged in an alpine creek just above the tree line. The water was then agitated by a wood nymph.</td>', 'For those, who wanted to know what it was: a branch of an old ebony tree carefully painted with leaf-gold placed on a slab of BC jade submerged in an alpine creek just above the tree line. The water was then agitated by a wood nymph.', '2003-09-11 14:14:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(416350, 35899, 6870, '<td valign="top">To Clues56: I simply held my camera in my right hand and the cob of corn in the other, pressed the cob against the bottom of the camera for stability, set a fairly deep DOF (actually I took about two dozen shots with varying depths of field). The entire shot was taken around 6 pm when the sun was still in the sky but fairly low, and I made sure that I was in the shade, with background stuff fairly far away. So my fancy lighting is the sun, but in the shade.</td>', 'To Clues56: I simply held my camera in my right hand and the cob of corn in the other, pressed the cob against the bottom of the camera for stability, set a fairly deep DOF (actually I took about two dozen shots with varying depths of field). The entire shot was taken around 6 pm when the sun was still in the sky but fairly low, and I made sure that I was in the shade, with background stuff fairly far away. So my fancy lighting is the sun, but in the shade.', '2003-09-12 00:46:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(417984, 35932, 12169, '<td valign="top">I didn''t realise that it was a slinky. I guess it worked on (for) me!</td>', 'I didn''t realise that it was a slinky. I guess it worked on (for) me!', '2003-09-13 15:05:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(418411, 35772, 472, '<td valign="top">meant to tell you what a cool picture this is.  the composition is what really makes it - the way you use the whole frame, yet there''s nothing extraneous.  great job.</td>', 'meant to tell you what a cool picture this is.  the composition is what really makes it - the way you use the whole frame, yet there''s nothing extraneous.  great job.', '2003-09-13 23:42:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(418418, 35369, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Very good perspective, excellent detail and texture.  Very good use of dof, only thing is the gutter draws your eye the whole way from bottom to top and I feel almost like there should be something at the end of it. <br/> <br/>As it is right now it is a bit dull and needs something more added to it, even if it was merely a leaf or a bit of trash at the end of the gutter.</td>', 'Critique Club Very good perspective, excellent detail and texture.  Very good use of dof, only thing is the gutter draws your eye the whole way from bottom to top and I feel almost like there should be something at the end of it.  As it is right now it is a bit dull and needs something more added to it, even if it was merely a leaf or a bit of trash at the end of the gutter.', '2003-09-14 00:07:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(418424, 35951, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Very interesting image definately fits the challenge well.  You may want to crop in tighter on it.  The one thing I do notice about it is it seems to be soft in spots but as I look closer I realize the yellow seem to be washed out slightly on the folds and it has given it that soft appearance. <br/> <br/>Very good and creative idea.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', '*Critique Club* Very interesting image definately fits the challenge well.  You may want to crop in tighter on it.  The one thing I do notice about it is it seems to be soft in spots but as I look closer I realize the yellow seem to be washed out slightly on the folds and it has given it that soft appearance.  Very good and creative idea. Anna', '2003-09-14 00:12:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(418582, 35913, 8367, '<td valign="top">The store was closing or I would have taken more shots. I wasn''t quite happy with the clarity(the lighting was awful)but I thought it met the challenge well. Each one of the TV monitors had different colors and it reminded me of our forum discussions pertaining to calibration. <br/>Thanks ellamay, EL-ROI, and xhoss for commenting.</td>', 'The store was closing or I would have taken more shots. I wasn''t quite happy with the clarity(the lighting was awful)but I thought it met the challenge well. Each one of the TV monitors had different colors and it reminded me of our forum discussions pertaining to calibration. Thanks ellamay, EL-ROI, and xhoss for commenting.', '2003-09-14 10:37:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(418670, 35118, 2700, '<td valign="top">This is a great example of what cropping and angle do for a pic. I "think" that if you were to crop out the ground, taken away the ladder, along with tilting the photo to the left about 3degrees (it seems "off", the boxes seem to be leaning to the right), you could be looking at a ribbon...</td>', 'This is a great example of what cropping and angle do for a pic. I "think" that if you were to crop out the ground, taken away the ladder, along with tilting the photo to the left about 3degrees (it seems "off", the boxes seem to be leaning to the right), you could be looking at a ribbon...', '2003-09-14 13:37:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(418671, 35914, 2700, '<td valign="top">very creative. I like</td>', 'very creative. I like', '2003-09-14 13:39:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(418745, 35559, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Hi Rob.<br/> <br/>I''ve sat here looking at this photo trying to decide what to say about it.  First off it doesn''t do much for me.  The macro itself is good with lots of detail and it does fit the challenge well, there is definately repetition in this photo so what is it I don''t like about the photo?  I think it lacks color and or tones. Possibly a little color behind the lace or try photographing it away from the window to get some tones and shadows into it.  <br/> <br/>As it is now you got a cool building ground for some neat abstracts by playing with color and tone and I seriously would play with it some.  It definately was able to hold my attention long enough to sit here since last night trying to figure out what I didn''t like about it and how to improve it.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', '*Critique Club* Hi Rob. I''ve sat here looking at this photo trying to decide what to say about it.  First off it doesn''t do much for me.  The macro itself is good with lots of detail and it does fit the challenge well, there is definately repetition in this photo so what is it I don''t like about the photo?  I think it lacks color and or tones. Possibly a little color behind the lace or try photographing it away from the window to get some tones and shadows into it.   As it is now you got a cool building ground for some neat abstracts by playing with color and tone and I seriously would play with it some.  It definately was able to hold my attention long enough to sit here since last night trying to figure out what I didn''t like about it and how to improve it. Anna', '2003-09-14 16:43:20.000000', NULL, 0),
